Amiga 500 for MEGA65 aka AExp
=============================

done in 2026 by sy2002    github.com/sy2002    www.sy2002.de

AExp is licensed under the terms of GNU/GPL v3, for more information
please read the file LICENSE. Parts of AExp are licensed under other
Free-software licenses as described in the source code.

Special thanks to deft for delivering a perfectly calibrated aexp_screen.cfg,
for providing the key mapping (doc/assets/doc/assets/keyboard.png) and for
testing and debugging hardware floppy disk reading.

Special thanks to dejavu4u2 for testing and debugging hardware floppy disk
reading and writing.

AExp:
-----

  AExp is a port of MiSTer's Minimig-AGA core, reduced in scope to an
  Amiga 500 with the OCS chipset,
      done by the MiSTer Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Minimig-AGA_MiSTer
      Significant contributors:
      * Alexey Melnikov (sorgelig)

  MiSTer's Minimig-AGA continues the Minimig ports for the MiST and
  Altera DE1 boards, which added the AGA chipset and many other features,
      Significant contributors:
      * Rok Krajnc
      * Tobias Gubener
      * Till Harbaum
      * A.M. Robinson

  Minimig is the original re-implementation of the Amiga in an FPGA,
      done by Dennis van Weeren in 2005-2007
      https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minimig
      Significant contributors:
      * Jakub Bednarski
      * Sascha Boing

  The 68000 CPU is fx68k, a cycle accurate implementation,
      done by Jorge Cwik
      https://github.com/ijor/fx68k

Other than that and my own work, AExp uses:
-------------------------------------------

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * QNICE Co-Processor and System-on-a-Chip for file operations and on-screen-menu by The QNICE Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/QNICE-FPGA

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by Paul Gardner-Stephen
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core, done by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto2

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI, done by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * Polyphase video scaling filter coefficients from the MiSTer project,
    taken from the collection curated for C64MEGA65
    https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Filters_MiSTer

  * HyperRAM controller, done by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * VGA Timing Generator, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/

The following resources were invaluable for developing AExp:
------------------------------------------------------------

  * Anthropic Fable 5 and Opus 4.8

  * The ARM-side Minimig support code of the MiSTer project (Main_MiSTer):
    the floppy disk protocol of this core follows its implementation
    https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Main_MiSTer
